From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:10:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Bound ARM64EC code map lookups on the PE side.

EcCodeBitMap has one bit per page of the 47-bit user address space.
RtlIsEcCode and arm64x_check_call index it with any address they are
given, so a kernel or non-canonical one (a corrupted unwind context, a
call through a bad pointer) reads far past the end of the map and
faults inside ntdll instead of answering "not EC code". RtlIsEcCode is
called from the unwinder (unwind.c) and the exception dispatcher, so
the fault lands in the code that was meant to recover from the first
one.

RtlIsEcCode returns FALSE for a NULL map or an address at or above
0x800000000000. arm64x_check_call checks the same bound before it loads
the map and sends such a target to .Lexit, the exit thunk: that is the
only safe branch, since the fall-through and .Ljmp paths read the
target's code from [x11] and would fault on it too. Jump destinations
come back through the start of the function and get the same check.

Adapted from Madeira (LGPL branch madeira-lgpl, by Will Faust):
ac650deca3 "ntdll: bounds-check RtlIsEcCode against non-canonical
pointers" for RtlIsEcCode, and the arm64x_check_call bound in
d88d55eee0, which shifts by 39 (its map coverage on iOS); here the map
covers 47 bits, so the shift is 47.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
index 1a8174e7..923ba889 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -1394,6 +1394,8 @@ BOOLEAN WINAPI RtlIsEcCode( ULONG_PTR ptr )
 {
     const UINT64 *map = (const UINT64 *)NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->EcCodeBitMap;
     ULONG_PTR page = ptr / page_size;
+    /* the map covers only the 47-bit user address space */
+    if (!map || ptr >= 0x800000000000) return FALSE;
     return (map[page / 64] >> (page & 63)) & 1;
 }
 
@@ -1899,6 +1901,8 @@ static void __attribute__((naked)) arm64x_check_call(void)
     asm( ".seh_proc \"#arm64x_check_call\"\n\t"
          ".seh_endprologue\n\t"
          /* check for EC code */
+         "lsr x16, x11, #47\n\t"            /* dest beyond the map: not EC code */
+         "cbnz x16, .Lexit\n\t"
          "ldr x16, [x18, #0x60]\n\t"        /* peb */
          "lsr x17, x11, #18\n\t"            /* dest / page_size / 64 */
          "ldr x16, [x16, #0x368]\n\t"       /* peb->EcCodeBitMap */
